  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "localId": "8c4835e2c6b1"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "We tried to use Camel Toolbox Fixity Checking Service (as described here: ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "localId": "772540a3135a",
        "url": "https://github.com/fcrepo-exts/fcrepo-camel-toolbox#fixity-checking-service"
       },
       "type": "inlineCard"
      },
      {
       "text": " ) but with many objects the queue will fill up, and Camel will stop to make checks. We used the service and have the fixity failure be handled by a script. The confs are here: ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "localId": "4d48dd1756c9",
        "url": "https://github.com/phaidra/phaidra/blob/main/camel-toolbox-config/configuration.properties"
       },
       "type": "inlineCard"
      },
      {
       "text": "  The script: ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "localId": "f96523f3a0c6",
        "url": "https://github.com/phaidra/phaidra/blob/main/scripts/fixity_handler.sh"
       },
       "type": "inlineCard"
      },
      {
       "text": "  just manage the output of camel to do the proper action, logging, etc. The problem is in Camel Toolbox Fixity Checking Service , after a while this happen:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "localId": "92f3e35d-1f89-48c7-8637-d6b22ffe1c19",
      "wrap": true
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "WARN 09:02:01.781 [ActiveMQ Transport: tcp:///xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx:41094@61616] (Queue) Usage(default:store:queue://fixity:store) percentUsage=0%, usage=1638041234, limit=1073741824, percentUsageMinDelta=1%;Parent:Usage(default:store) percentUsage=152%, usage=1638041234, limit=1073741824, percentUsageMinDelta=1%: Persistent store is Full, 100% of 1073741824. Stopping producer (ID:0df6362b43cd-45511-1784710534158-1:12:1:1) to prevent flooding queue://fixity. See http://activemq.apache.org/producer-flow-control.html  for more info (blocking for: 361s)",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "codeBlock"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "localId": "97fe09946f1b"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I've incremented the limits several time with a custom activemq.xml, but it reached the new limit and stuck again. Usually the checks starts very fast and over time they start to slow down.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "localId": "e98ddefb0b41"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Finally, using 48GB as storage size, I’ve been able to check fixity on 30M datastreams but I had to restart the Camel process once because checks was very slow. After the restart, checks were fast again. Moreover this error appears in the log, even if other threads work correctly and process queue messages:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "localId": "fa65344e-80e6-48c7-8afc-380721780702",
      "wrap": true
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "ERROR 07:21:31.627 [Camel (camel-1) thread #17 - JmsConsumer[reindexing]] (DefaultJmsMessageListenerContainer) Could not refresh JMS Connection for destination 'reindexing' - retrying using FixedBackOff{interval=5000, currentAttempts=2438, maxAttempts=unlimited}. Cause: Error while attempting to add new Connection to the pool; nested exception is javax.jms.JMSException: Could not connect to broker URL: tcp://fedora:61616. Reason: java.lang.IllegalStateException: Timer already cancelled.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "codeBlock"
    }
   ],
