     "body": "<p><font color=\"#ffffff\">I have confirmed that the issue is purely the value configured for storeUsage. I set up fedora 7 and camel toolbox and was able to reproduce your log errors. The reason it looks like messages are not being deleted on read is that camel reads 1 message and generates 2 more. one to send the file to fixity and another to traverse it to find any children. this multiplication gives the impression of not reducing the queue size but its actually just adding yet more messages to the already full store. Unfortunately, there is no single configuration that we can ship which suits every user. Some element of configuration at the activemq level will be required dependant on local requirements. This may be a case of better documentation being required, rather than a code/config fix</font></p>",
     "created": "Today 8:25 AM",
     "id": "29148",
